Through extensive debugging with debug output, I discovered:

1. Grammar items DO have 1 child in goal_value()
2. BUT their focus is undef (not evaluated)
3. The issue: When complete() updates the chart after evaluation (line 338), add_element() merges the NEW element (with evaluated focus) with the EXISTING element (with undef focus)
4. The add() operation was choosing self (existing element with undef focus) over other (new element with evaluated Grammar focus)

**The Fix**: Modified SemanticElement.add() to prefer elements with defined focus over undef focus:
```perl
# Prefer elements with evaluated focus (defined) over unevaluated (undef)
my $self_focus = $self->context->focus;
my $other_focus = $other->context->focus;

if (!defined($self_focus) && defined($other_focus)) {
    return $other;
}
if (defined($self_focus) && !defined($other_focus)) {
    return $self;
}
```

