### lib/Chalk/EvalContext.pm
**Why Important**: Implements the comonad pattern for semantic evaluation

**Key Methods**:
```perl
class Chalk::EvalContext {
    field $focus :param :reader;        # Current semantic value (the evaluated result)
    field $children :param :reader;     # Child contexts (array ref of sub-parse-trees)

    # Comonad operation: extract the focus value
    method extract() {
        return $focus;
    }

    # Convenience method: get extracted value of child at index
    method child($index) {
        return undef unless $index < scalar(@$children);
        return $children->[$index]->extract;  # Returns the child's focus
    }
}
```

### lib/Chalk/Grammar/BNF/Rule/Grammar.pm
**Why Important**: Semantic action for top-level Grammar rule - builds Chalk::Grammar object

**evaluate() method**:
```perl
method evaluate($context) {
    # Grammar -> LineList
    my $line_list = $context->child(0);  # Extract LineList's focus value

    my @rules = ref($line_list) eq 'ARRAY' ? @$line_list : ();
    @rules = grep { defined } @rules;  # Filter out undef (comments, blank lines)

    # Build grammar from collected rules
    my $grammar = Chalk::Grammar->build_grammar(rules => \@rules);
    return $grammar;  # This becomes the focus of the Grammar context
}
```

### lib/Chalk/Grammar/BNF/Rule/LineList.pm
**Why Important**: Accumulates lines into array, filtering out undefined values

**evaluate() method**:
```perl
method evaluate($context) {
    my @children = map { $_->extract } $context->children->@*;

    # LineList -> []  (empty)
    if (@children == 0) {
        return [];
    }

    # LineList -> Line  (single line)
    if (@children == 1) {
        my $line = $children[0];
        return defined($line) ? [$line] : [];
    }

    # LineList -> Line LineList  (multiple lines)
    if (@children == 2) {
        my ($line, $rest) = @children;
        my @result = ();
        push @result, $line if defined($line);
        push @result, @$rest if ref($rest) eq 'ARRAY';
        return \@result;
    }

    return [];
}
```

### lib/Chalk/Grammar/BNF/Rule/Line.pm
**Why Important**: Returns grammar rule or undef for comments/blank lines

**evaluate() method**:
```perl
method evaluate($context) {
    my @children = map { $_->extract } $context->children->@*;

    # Line -> GrammarRule '\n' or Line -> PatternDef '\n'
    # Return the first child (the actual content, not the newline)
    if (@children >= 1) {
        return $children[0];
    }

    # Line -> BlankLine or Line -> Comment '\n'
    # Return undef to signal this should be filtered out
    return undef;
}
```

