Now let me check the BNF grammar to understand how to add lowercase bareword support. The old parser in `lib/Chalk/BNF.pm` line 146 treats any bareword as a nonterminal:

```perl
elsif ( $rhs =~ /^([\w:]+|[^\s'\/]+)/ ) {
    push @tokens, $1;
```

But our hand-coded grammar only accepts capitalized identifiers as Nonterminals. Let me add a new rule for lowercase barewords that become string terminals:

